      "writtenOn": "2021-10-21T05:50:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Bundles are fairly expensive and error prone due to lack of type safety, string keys, etc. Why do you need it? Can\u0027t you just pass the PortBlockParcel itself inside msg.data? Or if not, maybe just define a simple static class with 3 public final members for port, ipType, and protocol, and use that?\n\nAlso, if you make the IPCs synchronous as suggested elsewhere, you probably don\u0027t need this.",
